# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stellify environment variables — EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL.
# With no file at all, Stellify runs fully in local-only mode: the whole question
# bank, lessons, mocks, analytics, pet and the offline tutor all work.
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in only what you want.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Optional: AI tutor enhancement (Google Gemini Developer API, free tier) ──
# Create a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey (no billing needed).
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Model to call. Free-tier model line-ups and quotas change; check
# https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing and your AI Studio rate-limit page.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest
# Comma-separated models tried in order if the first one is unavailable or rate limited.
GEMINI_MODEL_FALLBACKS=gemini-flash-lite-latest

# Stellify's own conservative caps so a free quota is never burned by one visitor.
TUTOR_RATE_PER_MINUTE=6
TUTOR_DAILY_CAP=150

# ── Optional: accounts + cloud sync (Supabase free tier) ─────────────────────
# Run supabase/schema.sql in your project first. The anon key is safe to expose:
# row-level security restricts every row to its owner.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Optional: static hosting under a sub-path (e.g. GitHub Pages project site) ─
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/aboutme
